<h1>Personal collection of (mostly free) fonts</h1>
<blockquote>Everyone has a favorite font, right? RIGHT!?</blockquote>

<p>This is just a personal and opinionated collection of fonts that stuck with me and started as an excuse to show off the <a href="https://github.com/elbym/font-collection/blob/main/font_specimen_generator.py">font_specimen_generator.py</a> (I asked Claude to cobble together). I switched to a <a href="https://elbym.github.io/font-collection/">HTML preview</a> instead.</p>
<p>This list is also influenced by <a hred="https://www.teuderun.de/schriftarten/top-10/">Teuderun</a> and <a href="https://typotheque.luuse.io/">Free Font Library</a> and <a href="https://typotheque.luuse.io/">the free fontlibrary.</a></p>


<p>The speciment poster is heavily inspired by (copied from) <a href="https://sammlungen.ub.uni-frankfurt.de/drucke/nav/classification/10736375">Schriftprobensammlung Gustav Mori</a> at the University of Frankfurt.</p>


<p>Why did i stumbel across this so late? <a href="https://www.forthehearts.net/about">Claus Eggers Sørensen</a> has wonderfull specimen layouts for his <a href="https://www.forthehearts.net/playfair">Playfair</a> font <a href="https://www.forthehearts.net/demonstration/Playfair2_Words.html">word tower Specimen Demo</a></p>

